      "sourceTextSha256": "ea1a5f07aa90165eea9b24afb2c2bef486cc7130cb5d62d809a3aed9856f0684",
      "text": "A tour of the Brazilian side of the falls (shared basis, English-speaking guide). On the border of Brazil, Argentina and Paraguay, within a national park of unique flora and fauna, 275 waterfalls, each with its own name, crash into the canyon of the Devil’s Throat; their name means “big water” in Guarani. The contrast between the calm, almost lazy river above the falls and the torrents boiling into the gorge below is stunning: you could watch this spectacle for hours.",
